sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-011: Platform-wide Looking-for-Team — Sequence Diagram
    actor User as Participant
    participant ReactUI
    participant FirebaseAuth
    participant ExpressAPI
    participant AvailabilityRepo
    participant PostgreSQL

    User->>ReactUI: Open Looking for Team page
    ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: GET /api/availability/me and GET /api/availability
    ExpressAPI->>FirebaseAuth: Verify token, MFA, active account, PART role, and verified email
    alt Visitor or ineligible account
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 401 or 403 with no candidate cards
        ReactUI-->>User: Sign-in or verification guidance
    else Verified PART
        ExpressAPI->>AvailabilityRepo: Read platform availability and active candidates
        AvailabilityRepo->>PostgreSQL: Query canonical platform-pool rows
        PostgreSQL-->>AvailabilityRepo: Preferences and active LFT records
        AvailabilityRepo-->>ExpressAPI: Platform records without client event input
        ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: Preferences plus permitted candidate projections
        ReactUI-->>User: Render toggle, form, and candidate cards
    end

    User->>ReactUI: Edit toggle, role, hours, and goal
    ReactUI->>ReactUI: Validate role, goal, and 0–168 hours
    alt Client validation fails
        ReactUI-->>User: Field errors with entered values preserved
    else Client validation succeeds
        ReactUI->>ExpressAPI: PUT /api/availability/me without eventId
        ExpressAPI->>ExpressAPI: Reject eventId or unknown fields and validate payload
        alt Server validation fails
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with field errors
            ReactUI-->>User: Preserve values and show errors
        else Valid update
            ExpressAPI->>AvailabilityRepo: Upsert by authenticated participant
            AvailabilityRepo->>PostgreSQL: Write canonical platform-pool row
            PostgreSQL-->>AvailabilityRepo: Updated availability
            AvailabilityRepo-->>ExpressAPI: Platform availability record
            ExpressAPI-->>ReactUI: 200 success
            ReactUI-->>User: Confirmation and refreshed candidate pool
        end
    end

    Note over AvailabilityRepo,PostgreSQL: event_availability.event_id stores a fixed internal Platform Availability Pool row for compatibility. The client never selects or submits it.

